invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_sp1 returns without wiping m1, which crt_combine left
  holding the difference of the two halves of the signature in p's
  domain. That difference with the signature gives a prime.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below one call and finds two
  limbs of the difference there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(em_plain, sizeof em_plain);
    ct_wipe(m1, sizeof m1);
--- new
    ct_wipe(em_plain, sizeof em_plain);
